{"id": "86374", "name": "Planes_find_equation_plane", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.5, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Determine the equation of the plane through the point \\(P\\) with coordinates {{CT:0}} and with normal vector \\(\\underline{n}\\) with components {{CT:1}}.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">Equation is: [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><p class=\"input-hint input-hint-equation\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.88em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0;text-align:left\">How to enter: with an <code dir=\"ltr\">=</code> sign, and multiplication with a star. For example <code dir=\"ltr\">2*x-y+3*z=4</code>.</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> A point \\(X=(x,y,z)\\) lies on the plane exactly when \\(X-P\\) is orthogonal to the normal vector, that is, \\(\\underline{n}\\cdot(X-P)=0\\), or equivalently \\(\\underline{n}\\cdot X=\\underline{n}\\cdot P\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The left-hand side</b><br>With \\(\\underline{n}={{CT:2}}\\) and \\(X=(x,y,z)\\):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\underline{n}\\cdot X={{CT:3}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The right-hand side</b><br>With \\(P={{CT:4}}\\):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\underline{n}\\cdot P=\\left({{CT:5}}\\right)\\left({{CT:6}}\\right)+\\left({{CT:7}}\\right)\\left({{CT:8}}\\right)+\\left({{CT:9}}\\right)\\left({{CT:10}}\\right)={{CT:11}} \\]</p>So the equation of the plane is<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:12}} \\]</p>The equation is not unique: multiplying both sides by the same nonzero number, or moving all terms to one side, gives an equation of the same plane.</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "determinant, invert", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["avar", "bvar", "correctanswer", "cvar", "solRHS", "vector1", "vector2", "wronganswer"], "nvariants": 50}